<article class="env-lemma" id="03J1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03J1">Lemma <span data-tag="03J1">28.30.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact scheme. There exists a dense open $V \subset X$ which is separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $X = \bigcup _{i = 1, \ldots , n} U_ i$ is a union of $n$ affine open subschemes. We will prove the lemma by induction on $n$. It is trivial for $n = 1$. Let $V' \subset \bigcup _{i = 1, \ldots , n - 1} U_ i$ be a separated dense open subscheme, which exists by induction hypothesis. Consider 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  V = V' \amalg (U_ n \setminus \overline{V'}).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       It is clear that $V$ is separated and a dense open subscheme of $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>